    "result_text": "The full suite is green (53 tests, 0 failures/errors).\n\n## Summary\n\nI updated `getMembershipLevel()` in `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java` to implement the tenure-based level 4.\n\n**What changed:** The method previously computed a level from two factors (email +1, no namesakes +1) and hard-capped the result at `3`, so level 4 was unreachable. I:\n\n- Added a tenure factor: `+1` when `registrationDate` is set and the owner's tenure \u2014 `ChronoUnit.DAYS.between(registrationDate, LocalDate.now())` \u2014 is **more than 365 days**.\n- Raised the cap from `3` to `4`.\n- Updated the Javadoc to describe the 1\u20134 range and the tenure rule.\n\n**Why it satisfies the spec:** A newly created owner has `registrationDate` = today, so its tenure is 0 days (not > 365), meaning the tenure factor never fires on creation. A new owner with an email and `namesakeCount` of 0 therefore maxes out at `1 + 1 + 1 = 3`, exactly as `Cp39Tests.coreNewOwnerCappedAtLevel3` expects. Household size does not contribute to the level, so a 3-member household stays at 3. Level 4 is only reachable once real tenure exceeds 365 days.\n\nThe new `Cp39Tests` and the existing membership tests (`Cp15`, `Cp23`, `Cp24`) all pass, and the complete suite builds green.",
